NOTICE — release image bundles provenance
=========================================

The archives attached to this repository's releases are convenience
redistributions of *unmodified* build artifacts, produced with
`tools/export-images.sh` (`docker save` / `split` — nothing repackaged,
rebased or modified inside the images).

They are derived from the following upstream works. Each remains under its
own license; nothing here changes those terms. If in doubt, obtain the
originals from the official sources listed below.

1. Container images (ci-images, vrnetlab-sonic-vs bundles)
   - Base: `sonicdev-microsoft.azurecr.io/sonic-slave-bookworm`, built by
     https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage (Apache License 2.0).
     The base image contains Debian GNU/Linux packages (each under its own
     license, per Debian) and other build tooling installed by the SONiC
     build system (including the Microsoft .NET SDK, distributed under its
     own terms).
   - Locally built layers on top of that base: `swss-bookworm-master`,
     `swsscommon-bookworm`, `sonic-ci-py3:base` — install the upstream
     CI dependency set (debs from sonic-net/sonic-swss-common,
     sonic-sairedis, sonic-buildimage common-libs; SONiC python wheels,
     Apache-2.0) into the base image. Dockerfiles are in `cicd/`.
   - `vrnetlab/sonic_sonic-vs` wraps the official SONiC VS image with
     vrnetlab (https://github.com/vrnetlab/vrnetlab) for container use.
   - Official pull source for the base image:
     `docker pull sonicdev-microsoft.azurecr.io:443/sonic-slave-bookworm:master-amd64`

2. SONiC VS nightly archive (sonic-vs.img.gz parts)
   - The official, unmodified SONiC master nightly `sonic-vs.img.gz`
     published by the SONiC build system
     (https://github.com/sonic-net/SONiC, Apache License 2.0; image contents
     under their respective licenses). Split as-is for the 2 GiB release
     asset limit; `cat` the parts to recover the identical gzip file.
   - Official download source:
     https://sonic-net.github.io/SONiC/sonic_latest_images.html
     (also automated by `vs/download-vs.sh`).

